  "description": "Reads HTML into a DocWright Word document and writes a Word document as HTML, with no third-party HTML or CSS library. A tolerant HTML5 parser recovers from malformed markup the way a browser does, applies a documented CSS subset, maps h1-h6 to heading styles and never fetches external resources; the writer produces one self-contained file (images as data URIs), linked images and stylesheet, or a body fragment. Most users should install the DocWright package instead, which includes this one.",
